title: World War Two
subject: History
level: GCSE
emoji: ✈️
description: From the invasion of Poland to VE and VJ Day.
---
When did WW2 begin in Europe? :: 1 September 1939, when Germany invaded Poland.
Why did Britain declare war on 3 September 1939? :: Germany did not withdraw from Poland, which Britain had promised to defend.
What was appeasement? :: Giving in to Hitler's demands to avoid war – associated with Neville Chamberlain.
What was the Munich Agreement (1938)? :: Britain and France allowed Germany to take the Sudetenland from Czechoslovakia.
What was Blitzkrieg? :: 'Lightning war' – fast combined attacks by tanks, aircraft and infantry.
What was Dunkirk? :: The evacuation of over 300,000 Allied troops from France in May–June 1940.
Who became British Prime Minister in May 1940? :: Winston Churchill.
What was the Battle of Britain (1940)? :: An air battle in which the RAF defeated the Luftwaffe, preventing invasion.
What was the Blitz? :: German bombing of British cities from September 1940 to May 1941.
What was Operation Barbarossa? :: Germany's invasion of the Soviet Union in June 1941.
What happened at Pearl Harbor? :: Japan attacked the US naval base on 7 December 1941, bringing the USA into the war.
Which battle was a major Soviet victory that turned the tide on the Eastern Front (1942–43)? :: Stalingrad.
Which battle in North Africa in 1942 was a turning point for Britain? :: El Alamein.
What was D-Day? :: The Allied invasion of Normandy on 6 June 1944.
What was the Holocaust? :: The Nazi genocide of six million Jews, as well as millions of others.
What was the Kindertransport? :: Rescue of nearly 10,000 mostly Jewish children from Nazi Europe to Britain (1938–40).
What was evacuation in Britain? :: Moving children from cities to the countryside to keep them safe from bombing.
What was rationing? :: Government limits on food and goods so supplies were shared fairly.
When was VE Day? :: 8 May 1945 – Victory in Europe.
What ended the war with Japan? :: Atomic bombs on Hiroshima and Nagasaki (August 1945); VJ Day was 15 August.
What was the Yalta Conference? :: February 1945 meeting of Churchill, Roosevelt and Stalin to plan post-war Europe.
